WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.093
<v Examiner>Case 11.

2
00:00:02.093 --> 00:00:02.946
<v Examiner>Lactation.

3
00:00:02.946 --> 00:00:03.799
<v Examiner>Six marks.

4
00:00:04.249 --> 00:00:08.051
<v Examiner>Pania is two days postpartum, and her milk is just coming in.

5
00:00:08.051 --> 00:00:12.475
<v Examiner>Two hormones are involved in the production and release of breast milk.

6
00:00:12.475 --> 00:00:18.021
<v Examiner>For each one, say where it's made or secreted from, what stimulates it, and its function.

7
00:00:18.021 --> 00:00:23.442
<v Examiner>Describe the structure of the mammary gland, and the path milk takes out of the breast.

8
00:00:23.442 --> 00:00:25.000
<v Examiner>What type of gland is it,

9
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.175
<v Examiner>and what happens to the breasts in pregnancy as progesterone rises?

10
00:00:29.625 --> 00:00:31.893
The second case she names for Test 3.

11
00:00:31.893 --> 00:00:36.981
It's long, but it's four small questions: the hormones, the gland, the milk's path,

12
00:00:36.981 --> 00:00:37.839
and pregnancy.

13
00:00:38.289 --> 00:00:41.011
The hook: prolactin, pro for produces.

14
00:00:41.011 --> 00:00:42.516
Oxytocin lets it out.

15
00:00:42.516 --> 00:00:44.881
And the baby suckling fires both.

16
00:00:45.331 --> 00:00:46.914
Hormone one: prolactin.

17
00:00:46.914 --> 00:00:49.667
It's secreted by the anterior pituitary.

18
00:00:49.667 --> 00:00:54.760
It stimulates milk production by the alveolar cells of the mammary glands.

19
00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:56.711
Hormone two: oxytocin.

20
00:00:56.711 --> 00:01:01.690
It's made in the hypothalamus, and released from the posterior pituitary.

21
00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:04.486
It stimulates milk release, the let-down,

22
00:01:04.486 --> 00:01:10.421
by making the myoepithelial cells around the alveoli contract and squeeze the milk out.

23
00:01:10.871 --> 00:01:12.239
What stimulates them?

24
00:01:12.239 --> 00:01:16.931
Both are released by a neural stimulus: the baby suckling at the breast.

25
00:01:16.931 --> 00:01:20.711
Let-down can also be set off by the baby's cry, its smell,

26
00:01:20.711 --> 00:01:22.796
or just thinking about the baby.

27
00:01:24.246 --> 00:01:24.883
The gland.

28
00:01:24.883 --> 00:01:27.494
Mammary glands are modified sweat glands.

29
00:01:27.494 --> 00:01:32.207
Each breast has fifteen to twenty-five lobes, radiating around the nipple.

30
00:01:32.207 --> 00:01:36.919
Each lobe has smaller lobules, and the lobules hold the glandular alveoli,

31
00:01:36.919 --> 00:01:38.193
which make the milk.

32
00:01:38.193 --> 00:01:40.868
The pigmented areola surrounds the nipple,

33
00:01:40.868 --> 00:01:45.771
and suspensory ligaments attach the breast to the fascia of the chest muscle.

34
00:01:46.221 --> 00:01:50.936
The milk's path out: alveoli, then alveolar ducts, then lactiferous ducts,

35
00:01:50.936 --> 00:01:52.401
then out at the nipple.

36
00:01:52.401 --> 00:01:55.651
Alveoli, alveolar ducts, lactiferous ducts, nipple.

37
00:01:56.101 --> 00:02:00.837
And in pregnancy: rising progesterone develops the lobules and alveoli.

38
00:02:00.837 --> 00:02:02.772
Those are the milk factories.

39
00:02:02.772 --> 00:02:05.241
Oestrogen grows the ducts, the pipes.

40
00:02:05.241 --> 00:02:10.778
Before pregnancy the ducts are there, but not the glandular tissue that makes milk.

41
00:02:12.228 --> 00:02:12.945
The traps.

42
00:02:12.945 --> 00:02:17.031
Swapping prolactin and oxytocin is the classic lost mark.

43
00:02:17.031 --> 00:02:19.612
Prolactin produces, oxytocin ejects.

44
00:02:19.612 --> 00:02:22.480
Second: the two halves of the pituitary.

45
00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:24.918
Prolactin comes from the anterior.

46
00:02:24.918 --> 00:02:29.865
Oxytocin is made in the hypothalamus and released from the posterior.

47
00:02:29.865 --> 00:02:34.095
Third: they're modified sweat glands, not sebaceous glands.

48
00:02:34.545 --> 00:02:35.144
<v Examiner>Once more.

49
00:02:35.144 --> 00:02:38.982
<v Examiner>Pania's two hormones, the gland, the milk's path, and pregnancy.

50
00:02:41.432 --> 00:02:47.301
Prolactin, from the anterior pituitary, stimulates the alveolar cells to produce milk.

51
00:02:47.301 --> 00:02:52.556
Oxytocin, made in the hypothalamus and released from the posterior pituitary,

52
00:02:52.556 --> 00:02:56.173
makes the myoepithelial cells contract: the let-down.

53
00:02:56.173 --> 00:02:58.903
Both are triggered by the baby suckling.

54
00:02:58.903 --> 00:03:01.905
The mammary gland is a modified sweat gland:

55
00:03:01.905 --> 00:03:08.047
fifteen to twenty-five lobes around the nipple, lobules of milk-making alveoli, an areola,

56
00:03:08.047 --> 00:03:09.753
and suspensory ligaments.

57
00:03:09.753 --> 00:03:13.916
Milk goes alveoli, alveolar ducts, lactiferous ducts, nipple.

58
00:03:13.916 --> 00:03:19.990
In pregnancy, progesterone builds the lobules and alveoli, and oestrogen grows the ducts.
